course: dictionary
lesson: 1450
title: Many meanings in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, so context tells you which one the writer means. The words around carve are the clues. «The sculptor will carve a lion from a block of stone.» The clues are sculptor and stone, so carve means cut hard material into a shape.
explain: «Dad will carve the turkey at the table.» Turkey is food, and Dad is at the table, so carve means cut cooked meat into slices. It does not mean making a statue. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
explain: Carve can also mean wearing something away over a long time. «Rivers carve valleys by wearing away rock.» The river is not using a knife. It slowly shapes the land, so carve here means shape something by cutting or wearing it away.
fact: Carve means to cut wood, stone, ice or another hard material carefully to make a shape or pattern.
fact: «Carved in stone» means something that can never change.
fact: «The Great Sphinx» is a huge statue carved from rock next to the pyramids.
fact: Glaciers are huge rivers of ice that carve deep valleys shaped like the letter U.
fact: Chinese printers carved wooden blocks to print books over 1,100 years ago.
exercise: «The sculptor will carve a lion from a block of stone.» What does carve mean here? | *To cut hard material into a shape | To wrap in paper | To cook slowly | To throw away
exercise: «Dad will carve the turkey at the table.» What does carve mean here? | To dig a hole | To paint a picture | *To cut cooked meat into slices | To wrap in paper
exercise: Which of these would a pupil carve in an art lesson? | A cloud in the sky | A glass of milk | *A bar of soap | A bike wheel
test:
«Their names were carved on the base of the statue.» What does carved mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Lost in the crowd | *Cut into the surface | Hidden under a blanket
«Rivers carve valleys by wearing away rock.» What does carve mean here? | Build with bricks | *Shape the land slowly by wearing it away | Paint a picture | Freeze solid
exam: A pupil reads «The promise was carved in stone.» What does this suggest? | It can change next week | *It can never change | It was only a joke | It was written in pencil
